                <pb facs="0643" n="541" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg541"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2559: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Tenney</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-26T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 26,
                                1919, 6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 26, 11.41 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of November 20, 10 p.m. The loan agreement has been
                    signed and the money turned over: Japanese offer rejected.</p>
                <p>Premier has given me letter of greeting to Mr. Lansing expressing hope of closer
                    future relations between the United States and China. Will forward letter by the
                    next pouch.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tenney</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
